• I found a more fundamental issue than the print lowering itself: the indexed-array state model currently conflates the
  storage register with the current SSA value. That means later reads in the same process can see the old reg instead of
  the just-assigned value. I’m patching that representation first, because it directly affects post-call state reads and
  loop-driven output.

