• The ADPCM mutable-reg path is fixed end to end.

  I repaired the MLIR/FSM handling in internal/mlir/emitter.go so mutable globals and array elements are treated
  consistently:

  - mutable module storage is emitted as sv.reg when FSM lowering is active
  - mutable reg reads go through sv.read_inout
  - FSM-side AssignOperation updates become sv.passign only for real module-backed regs
  - non-storage AssignOperation values stay as SSA aliases instead of being dropped
  - root/module port names are preserved so ports like test_data_* are not misclassified as inout regs

  I also added an MLIR regression in internal/mlir/emitter_test.go to check that mutable regs are read with
  sv.read_inout while input ports are not. For the benchmark transcript itself, tests/CHStone/adpcm/main.go now prints
